WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.962
Findings go to the issue tracker without
names; that's this workbook's guidance.

2
00:00:04.962 --> 00:00:08.283
A drafted issue holds
the check, the severity,

3
00:00:08.283 --> 00:00:11.513
the object ID, the issue
and the fingerprint.

4
00:00:11.513 --> 00:00:16.174
It leaves out the object's name, which
for most checks is a user principal name.

5
00:00:16.174 --> 00:00:19.662
The evidence store is
access-controlled and holds the names;

6
00:00:19.662 --> 00:00:22.800
the tracker is read by more
people and doesn't need them.

7
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.750
A first run is a baseline, so it
opens one summary issue, not hundreds.

8
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:28.925
Then the package.

9
00:00:28.925 --> 00:00:33.007
It holds the kit run as written,
the drift report and summary,

10
00:00:33.007 --> 00:00:37.422
the latest provenance from the
other kits, an evidence manifest,

11
00:00:37.422 --> 00:00:41.087
and a SHA256SUMS file that
sha two fifty-six sum reads.

12
00:00:41.087 --> 00:00:45.952
Each manifest records the previous
package's manifest hash, so the packages

13
00:00:45.952 --> 00:00:50.200
form a chain, and a replaced package
or a missing day shows as a break.

14
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.912
The packager doesn't sign.

15
00:00:51.912 --> 00:00:57.134
Microsoft Learn's page on immutable
storage says a locked time-based retention

16
00:00:57.134 --> 00:00:59.586
policy lets blobs be created and read,

17
00:00:59.586 --> 00:01:03.770
but not modified or deleted,
until the retention interval ends.
